Subject: wxGTK: don't turn a printable key into Escape, Tab, Return or Backspace

For a key whose keysym is a non-letter character, wxTranslateGTKKeyEventToWx()
takes the key code from what the key with the same hardware code produces in
a fixed US layout, so that keys give the same codes as on a US keyboard
whatever the layout. That assumes the current keymap uses the standard evdev
key codes. A keymap that numbers its keys in its own way breaks it: wtype, for
one, gives the first character it types the code 9, which is Escape in the US
layout. Typing "3" with it then sent a key down event with WXK_ESCAPE, and a
dialog with an escape id closed on it.

Only take the US layout's character when it is printable. Otherwise fall back
on the key's own Unicode value, as the code already does without XKB.

Not upstream as of wxWidgets v3.3.4 and master 2026-10-13: both have the same
code.
---
diff --git a/src/gtk/window.cpp b/src/gtk/window.cpp
index 78c1dd8b04..2d6d116732 100644
--- a/src/gtk/window.cpp
+++ b/src/gtk/window.cpp
@@ -1191,7 +1191,17 @@ wxTranslateGTKKeyEventToWx(wxKeyEvent& event,
                                    gdk_event->hardware_keycode,
                                    key_code_str,
                                    sizeof(key_code_str));
-            if ( strlen(key_code_str) == 1 )
+
+            // The hardware code is the same physical key as in the US layout
+            // only when the current keymap uses the standard evdev key codes.
+            // A keymap that numbers its keys in its own way, as virtual
+            // keyboards do (wtype, on-screen keyboards, remote input), can
+            // send a printable character on a code that is Escape, Tab,
+            // Return or Backspace in the US layout. A character key must not
+            // turn into one of those, so only take the US layout's character
+            // when it is printable too.
+            const unsigned char usChar = key_code_str[0];
+            if ( strlen(key_code_str) == 1 && usChar >= 0x20 && usChar != 0x7f )
             {
                 extraTraceInfo = " [XKB]";
 
@@ -1226,8 +1236,9 @@ wxTranslateGTKKeyEventToWx(wxKeyEvent& event,
             else
 #endif // wxHAS_XKB
             {
-                // Without XKB we can only fall back on using the Unicode key
-                // code if possible.
+                // Without XKB, or when the US layout gives no printable
+                // character for this key, we can only fall back on using the
+                // Unicode key code if possible.
                 if ( unichar < 256 )
                 {
                     key_code = unichar;
